<title>ITALY: TIM WINS MOBILE PHONE LICENCES IN BRAZIL.</title>
<headline>TIM WINS MOBILE PHONE LICENCES IN BRAZIL.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's mobile phone company Telecom Italia Mobile (TIM) said on Thursday that its international mobile phone division, STET Mobile Holding, has been awarded mobile phone licences in two Brazilian states.</p>
<p>STET Mobile Holding is operating with Gruppo Vicunha and a union of Globopar and Bradesco in a consortium to operate in the Brazilian states in Bahia and Sergipe. The winning consortium has paid a first tranche of $90 million, which amounts to around 40 percent of the total licence price, a TIM statement said.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
</text>
